# Ignore everything
*

# Files to un-ignore
!.gitignore
!.gitmodules
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!CMakeLists.txt
!usplayer.code-workspace
!psiddrv.a65
!Makefile

# File types to un-ignore
!*.cmake
!*.cpp
!*.c
!*.h
!*.yml
!*.js
!*.wasm
!*.html
!*.bin

# Directories to un-ignore
!.github
!.github/workflows
!assets
!assets/cia6526_example
!assets/cia6526_example/**
!assets/tests
!assets/tests/**
!cmake
!src
!src/**
!lib
!lib/driver
# Vendored third party sources, which have to be in the repository and not just
# on a developer's disk: CMake decides whether software audio exists by looking
# for lib/residfp/siddefs-fp.h.in, so a checkout without these silently builds
# with US_HAVE_RESIDFP=0 and ships a player with no --output=audio, no --output=wav
# and no browser audio at all. That is what CI was doing.
#
# reSIDfp also carries a local patch (USP_NO_THREADS, see FilterModelConfig6581.cpp
# and 8580.cpp), so re-downloading the pristine tarball in CI would not be
# equivalent: the WEB build needs the patch or it aborts at runtime with
# "thread constructor failed".
!lib/residfp
!lib/residfp/**
!lib/miniaudio
!lib/miniaudio/**
# Nuked OPL3 1.8, the FM/OPL side of a SID+FM tune. Two self contained C files,
# GPLv2 or later, vendored for the same reason reSIDfp is: the command line
# player and the browser have to run the *same* engine, or the same tune sounds
# different depending on where it is played.
!lib/nukedopl
!lib/nukedopl/**
# The un-ignore rules above are per extension, and these are the ones the
# vendored trees use that nothing else does.
!*.h.in
!*.cc
!COPYING
!roms
!tests
!web

# Generated into web/ by the WEB build, see CMakeLists.txt.
# The rules above un-ignore *.js and *.wasm, which would otherwise pull the
# build's own output into the repository.
web/usbsid.js
web/usbsid.mjs
# The same module again under a name every server serves as JavaScript.
web/usbsid.esm.js
web/usbsid.wasm
# Ignore test docs
web/README.md
web/bench.html
web/usbsid-diag.html
